<section class="content-section"><div class="container"><div class="row g-4"><div class="col-lg-7"><article class="surface-card prose"><span class="eyebrow">OUR PURPOSE</span><h2 class="mt-1">A healthier coast starts with all of us.</h2><p>Bantay Dagat Marinduque connects residents, fishers, visitors, and local response teams. This platform provides a place to report coastal concerns, follow report progress, learn about marine life, and find community conservation updates.</p><h2>Our mission</h2><p>To promote the protection and preservation of Marinduque's coastal and marine resources through community participation, environmental awareness, and effective incident reporting.</p><h2>Our vision</h2><p>To establish a cleaner, safer, and more sustainable coastal environment for the future generations of Marinduque.</p><h2>Our objectives</h2><ul><li>Make community incident reporting accessible and responsible.</li><li>Support timely review and coordination by authorized Bantay Dagat personnel.</li><li>Share useful marine conservation information and local announcements.</li><li>Encourage collaboration to protect coastal habitats and livelihoods.</li></ul></article></div><div class="col-lg-5"><div class="surface-card mb-4"><span class="eyebrow">HOW REPORTING WORKS</span><h2 class="h5 fw-bold">From observation to action</h2><ol class="text-secondary small lh-lg ps-3"><li>Share an incident description and location.</li><li>Keep the reference number provided after submission.</li><li>Authorized personnel review and update its status.</li><li>Check report progress using the reference number.</li></ol><a class="btn btn-primary rounded-pill" href="report.php">Report a coastal issue</a></div><div class="privacy-callout" id="privacy"><b>Privacy & responsible reporting</b><br>Reporter names, email addresses, phone numbers, and evidence are restricted to authorized administrators and are never shown on public tracking or map views. Do not report emergencies through this website alone; contact local emergency services directly.</div></div></div><div class="row g-4 mt-2"><div class="col-md-4"><div class="activity-card"><i class="fa-solid fa-water text-primary fs-4"></i><h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-3">Healthy seas</h3><p class="help-text mb-0">Marine ecosystems sustain biodiversity, livelihoods, and community well-being.</p></div></div><div class="col-md-4"><div class="activity-card"><i class="fa-solid fa-people-group text-primary fs-4"></i><h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-3">Community role</h3><p class="help-text mb-0">Local observations help identify issues early and guide responsible response.</p></div></div><div class="col-md-4"><div class="activity-card"><i class="fa-solid fa-seedling text-primary fs-4"></i><h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-3">Shared responsibility</h3><p class="help-text mb-0">Everyday choices and community activities can help protect coastal habitats.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
